    "spine_order": "3",
    "value_type": "scalar",
    "unit": "currency/month",
    "threshold_unit": null,
    "label": {
      "en": "Basic insurance pension: tscsepi and tscse"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$BasicPens"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "$BasicPens (355.81 EUR/month in the latest system year, updated across 18 dated values since 2005) is Lithuania's 'basic pension' reference amount within the state social-insurance pension system. It feeds boa00_lt's BenCalc function (Comp_perTU, 'recalculate bdict' step) — a policy whose name suggests it computes a basic/state old-age pension component — and also tscse_lt's ArithOp and BenCalc functions ('1a) pension insurance' and '1b) those with self-employment income and operating under business certificate: pension insurance'), where the label indicates it underlies the flat pension-insurance contribution owed by self-employed persons and business-certificate holders, who in Lithuania pay pension-insurance contributions calculated from a reference amount rather than from actual income. No theme-doc or country-report source for pensions was available for this batch, so the description relies on the constant's label and its citing functions."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: Pension age, MMS, AMS, AMSp,  BSA, SSI, CYI, CBN, basic/asistance pensions bases, RP"
    },
    "last_confirmed_valid_on": null,
    "temporal_basis": "in_force"
  },
